---
import '../styles/ironworks.css';

const repos = [
  { label: 'mnemra/mnemra-core', url: 'https://github.com/mnemra/mnemra-core', blurb: 'The engine Mnemra will run on.' },
  { label: 'mnemra/governance', url: 'https://github.com/mnemra/governance', blurb: 'Governs how Mnemra is developed.' },
];
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">

  <title>Mnemra — context layer for MCP</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Context and memory for agents and the people they work with. Nothing is released yet: Mnemra will be a single binary that agents reach over MCP. Apache-2.0.">

  <!-- Open Graph / social share -->
  <meta property="og:title" content="Mnemra — context layer for MCP">
  <meta property="og:description" content="Context and memory for agents and the people they work with. Nothing is released yet: Mnemra will be a single binary that agents reach over MCP. Apache-2.0.">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://mnemra.dev">
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://mnemra.dev/og.png">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="Mnemra — context layer for MCP">
  <meta name="twitter:description" content="Context and memory for agents and the people they work with. Nothing is released yet: Mnemra will be a single binary that agents reach over MCP. Apache-2.0.">

  <!-- Fonts: Ironworks families from Google Fonts -->
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cinzel:wght@600;700;900&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@300;400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

  <!-- Favicon -->
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png">
  <link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="Blog — Mnemra" href="/rss.xml">
</head>

<body>
  <main class="container">

    <div class="site-header blog-nav">
      <a href="/blog">Blog</a>
    </div>

    <!-- Avatar: Cinzel M on near-black, Ironworks nameplate -->
    <svg class="avatar" viewBox="0 0 400 400" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Mnemra">
      <title>Mnemra</title>
      <rect width="400" height="400" fill="#1a1612" rx="4" ry="4"/>
      <radialGradient id="glow" cx="50%" cy="46%" r="55%">
        <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#2a2219" stop-opacity="0.9"/>
        <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#1a1612" stop-opacity="0"/>
      </radialGradient>
      <rect width="400" height="400" fill="url(#glow)"/>
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="400" height="2" fill="#b08d57"/>
      <rect x="0" y="398" width="400" height="2" fill="#8a6a35" fill-opacity="0.6"/>
      <text x="200" y="258" font-family="Cinzel, Georgia, serif" font-weight="700" font-size="280" text-anchor="middle" fill="#d4af70">M</text>
      <rect x="130" y="296" width="140" height="2" fill="#b08d57"/>
      <polygon points="200,314 206,320 200,326 194,320" fill="#b08d57" fill-opacity="0.75"/>
    </svg>

    <div class="eyebrow">Context Layer &mdash; MCP</div>
    <h1>MNEMRA</h1>
    <p class="pronunciation">pronounced NEM-ra</p>

    <div class="body-copy">
      <p><strong>Context and memory for the agents and people working the same problems.</strong> Every session starts cold, so the orchestrating agent hand-loads the context again each time, and it drifts. Mnemra will keep that context alive between sessions; it's meant to be that layer, built once, so each team doesn't rebuild it.</p>
      <p>Agents will reach it over MCP. Self-host is planned as a single binary with Postgres built in, one instance per team. Going past that changes more than where the data sits: that deployment needs its own Postgres, and a permissions model for work that crosses teams. We haven't worked out what else it takes. None of it has shipped yet; agent communication is the piece being built now. Apache-2.0.</p>
    </div>

    <a href="/blog" class="hero-blog-link">Read the blog &rarr;</a>

    <h2 class="eyebrow">Planned</h2>
    <ol class="fragments">
      <li>Agents addressing each other, and handing work between them.</li>
      <li>Projects, tasks and repositories, so agents and people read one record of the work.</li>
      <li>One MCP call returns an artifact's cross-session context, with hybrid search and typed links.</li>
      <li>A first load of what a team already has, then ingest that keeps running.</li>
      <li>Further out, reports over all of it, including ones you define and call as MCP tools.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="repos">
      <h2 class="eyebrow">On GitHub, no release yet</h2>
      <ul class="repo-list">
        {repos.map((repo) => (
          <li class="repo-list-item">
            <a href={repo.url} class="repo-link" rel="noopener">
              <span class="repo-label">{repo.label}</span>
              <span class="repo-blurb">{repo.blurb}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!--
      Subscribe form. Buttondown embed endpoint.
      If submissions fail, swap buttondown.com -> buttondown.email (legacy domain still served during migration).
    -->
    <form class="cta-row"
          action="https://buttondown.com/api/emails/embed-subscribe/peter.manahan"
          method="post"
          target="popupwindow"
          onsubmit="window.open('https://buttondown.com/peter.manahan', 'popupwindow')">
      <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="your@email" aria-label="Email address" required>
      <button type="submit">Subscribe</button>
    </form>
    <p class="cta-microcopy">New posts by email. Project news rides along.</p>

    <div class="footer">
      <div class="status-line">Built in the open</div>
      <div class="social">
        <a href="https://github.com/mnemra">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/mnemra.dev">Bluesky</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/mnemra">LinkedIn</a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </main>
</body>
</html>
